    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0351" n="339" xml:id="pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.154A/7–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-08T16:00:00+03:25">July 8, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 8—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>485. From Hoskins.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d341-f1"/> Reference Legation’s 429,
                    June 15.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d341-f2"/> Millspaugh, Black and Shields
                    seriously disturbed over impending withdrawal of American military personnel
                    from Iranian Road Transport Administration. Although General Connolly has
                    acquiesced in token releases for June and July, balance of men must be released
                    by August 26 unless orders are changed.</p>
                <p>How soon can we expect word from Landis as to results of his efforts with War
                    Department for continued service of these men in this vital work? They are
                    needed until January 1 if firm operating foundation is to be laid and at least
                    until November 15 when critical harvest collection period will be largely past.
                    Sent to Department as 485; repeated to Cairo for Short. [Hoskins.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d341-f1" n="77" xml:id="d341-f1-content">
                <p>Harold B. Hoskins, Head of Middle East Supply Center at Tehran.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d341-f2" n="78" xml:id="d341-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Chargé had reported that General Connolly had “raised question
                    of release of American military personnel serving with Iranian Road Transport
                    Administration.” (891.154A/6–1544)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
